# Scoops an escape pod, and meets a boulder the scoops cannot take. It starts from scooping-an-escape-pod.cdr
# (Tools/PrepareCommanders.py): the commander mining-laser.replay starts from, with fuel scoops and a mining laser, but
# with the random state 154,538 draws on, which spawns an escape pod 10,000 units ahead in the first second of space.
# Steered to pass under the nose, as scooping-a-canister.replay's barrel is, it is scooped (TryScoopObject): Escape Pod
# Retrieved...Slaves!, a tonne of slaves into the hold. A boulder spawns next; steered under the nose too, it shows
# SCOOP RETRIEVAL INACTIVE, then rams the ship and is destroyed, for a bounty of 0.1 credits. The draw count was found
# by a search of 1,000 counts for the soonest escape pod scooped; the flight was played by the scratch program
# mining-laser.replay's was, and what it pressed is recorded here.
file JAMESON.CDR scooping-an-escape-pod.cdr
wait 0.5; key space; wait 3.5      # any key: the credits, then the status screen
key Escape; wait 0.3               # the disc menu
key l; wait 0.3                    # Load Commander: it asks for a file name
key j; key a; key m; key e; key s; key o; key n; key Return; wait 0.5
digest loaded 3dac45093ed08f77f4a3a95b2a73b2475048a855771814f5c2c9e57d3c103153
key F1; wait 1                     # launch
# The flight, as recorded: a step for each change of the keys, and the frames between.
down period; down Up; wait 0.350
up period; wait 0.600
down Right; up Up; down Down; wait 0.050
digest escape-pod c8a6372c649acfe501302c50eb16be64f2e551100d377c165b654f1b2ee95889
